---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE, ACTIVE_CATEGORIES } from '../site.config';
---

<PageLayout
  title="About Us"
  subtitle={`Who we are, what we cover and why ${SITE.name} exists`}
  description={`${SITE.name} tracks government exam notifications, admit cards and results, and explains government schemes, important tech news and cinema updates, for students and job seekers in India.`}
>
  <p>
    <strong>{SITE.name}</strong> is an independent website for students and job seekers in India. We track
    government job notifications, admit cards, answer keys and results, and we explain government schemes and the
    tech news that actually matters, in plain language: what happened, what the key dates are, who it affects, and what to do next.
    We also cover cinema: new releases in theatres and on OTT, trailers, box office and awards.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we started</h2>
  <p>
    Government exam updates are scattered across dozens of official websites and long notification PDFs, and the
    news usually reaches people through WhatsApp forwards that are late, incomplete or simply wrong. Government
    schemes have the same problem, with fake "yojana" messages everywhere. Tech news has
    the opposite problem: too much noise and hype, and not enough explanation of what a change means for you.
    Movie news is similar, full of rumoured release dates and inflated box office numbers, so we stick to what the
    makers and platforms officially announce.
  </p>
  <p>
    We wanted one place that gives you the correct facts from the official source, quickly, with a clear
    explanation. That's what {SITE.name} is for.
  </p>

  <h2>What we cover</h2>
  <div class="info-grid">
    {Object.entries(ACTIVE_CATEGORIES).map(([key, cat]) => (
      <div class="info-card">
        <h3><a href={`/category/${key}`}>{cat.name}</a></h3>
        <p>{cat.description}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2>Who writes here</h2>
  <div class="about-author">
    <img src={SITE.author.photo} alt={SITE.author.name} width="120" height="120" />
    <div>
      <p class="about-author-name">{SITE.author.name}</p>
      <p>{SITE.author.bio}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>
    We write the kind of update we'd want to read ourselves: accurate, specific, and without the fluff.
  </p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Official sources first.</strong> Dates, fees, eligibility rules, vacancies and prize amounts come from the organiser or the official notification, and every post links to it.</li>
    <li><strong>Checked before publishing.</strong> Every fact is checked against the official source and every post is reviewed before it goes live.</li>
    <li><strong>Our own take.</strong> We add what official pages don't tell you: who should apply, how to prepare, common mistakes and what happened in previous years.</li>
    <li><strong>Kept up to date.</strong> When a deadline is extended or results come out, we update the post and show the "Updated" date.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Read the full details in our <a href="/editorial-policy">Editorial Policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We don't charge students anything, and we never ask for fees or personal details to "register" you for anything.</li>
    <li>We don't promote earning apps, betting, crypto trading or "guaranteed income" schemes.</li>
    <li>We don't copy other websites' posts or images.</li>
    <li>We don't link to piracy sites or leaked movie prints, and we don't post spoilers without a clear warning.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Not an official website</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is not connected to any government department, exam conducting body, university
    or any company we write about. We're an independent information site. Always confirm details on the official
    website before you apply or pay any fee.
  </p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Found a mistake, know an opportunity we should cover, or want to collaborate? Write to
    {' '}<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or use our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
